# Retrospective transcript summary, backfilled for issue #355 (full backfill
# follow-up to the #352 sample), distilling PR #315's own body/commit history --
# no live session context was available (this PR predates or was outside this
# backfill session), per docs/plans/TRANSCRIPT_SUMMARY_GUIDELINES.md's
# retrospective case. Timestamps are real, from `gh pr view 315 --json
# commits,mergedAt`: startedAtTime is the first commit's authoredDate, endedAtTime is the PR's actual mergedAt.

ghpull:315 a bl:PullRequest, bl:WorkItem ;
    rdfs:label "fix(shacl): resolve literal sh:targetNode values as node-shape focus nodes" ;
    bl:number 315 ;
    bl:state bl:Closed ;
    bl:closesIssue ghissues:310 .

session:claudeSonnet5 a prov:SoftwareAgent ;
    rdfs:label "Claude Sonnet 5" .

session:pr315 a agp:AgentSession ;
    prov:wasAssociatedWith session:claudeSonnet5 ;
    prov:used ghissues:310 ;
    prov:startedAtTime "2026-07-31T09:24:40Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:endedAtTime "2026-07-31T16:36:04Z"^^xsd:dateTime .

session:pr315Summary a agp:TranscriptSummary ;
    agp:summaryText "data_targets()'s lookup_elem() silently dropped ElemValue::Literal, so a node shape's literal-valued sh:targetNode (e.g. sh:targetNode \"aldi\"^^xsd:integer) never became a focus node. This under-counted (or, when the literal was the only nonconforming target, false-negatived) node-shape-scoped (pathless) value constraints. Fixed by delegating lib.rs::lookup_elem to evaluate::lookup_elem_value (already correct, from #260), plus interning every Target::Node literal into the data view validate() reads from (needed because the W3C fixtures load one file as both shapes+data graph, which coincidentally hides this gap — a genuinely separate shapes/data pair does not). A related fix: node-shape-scoped sh:nodeKind violations reported sh:value as nil instead of the focus node itself (same pattern already fixed for sh:and/sh:or/sh:not/sh:xone by #309/#316). Correction to earlier scope claim An earlier revision of this PR claimed \"single root cause, not per-component: fixes all 15 core/node W3C SHACL suite entries previously skip-listed under 310.\" That claim was wrong — it was never verified against actual CI output. Proper triage (starting with datatype-001, as #310 asked) found the literal-sh:targetNode bug only accounts for 8 of the 15 listed entries." ;
    agp:reasoningFor ghpull:315 ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy session:pr315 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo session:claudeSonnet5 .
